        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-103295",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\n- The vertical asymptotes of the function are $x=2n\\pi $\n- Its graph passes through the point $(0,0)$\n- $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=tan⁡(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{6})$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/c2/c2d0606829588b01f6cba2fa4785b201c47a6d9ffa325d54e64544c9769d7e4a.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the graph of the function passes through the point $(0,0).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\pi )=tan⁡(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{6}).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."
      },
